MAJOR gap (all modes), distinct from the part-(c) transitive-extern fix (fcb0dcbc): a cross-package generic body that INSTANTIATES another package's generic, where the consumer imports neither the inner generic's package nor its deps. main imports only genlib; genlib.Sum[T] (generic) calls mid.F[T] (mid's generic), which calls deep.G(). main cannot monomorphize mid.F[int] because mid's generic DECL is not registered in the consumer (mid is a transitive, not direct, import — RegisterImports stashes generic decls only for direct imports; RegisterFuncExterns skips generic decls), so the inner instantiation resolves to an EMPTY mangled name: native "use of undefined value '@bn_main__'", VM "extern not found: main.". This is a TRANSITIVE GENERIC-DECL availability gap (Slice 7 completeness), deeper than the transitive-extern (part c) fix which only covers non-generic cross-pkg calls. Fix needs the consumer to stash the transitive closure of generic-bearing packages' generic decls (+ their defining files, for the import overlay), so a generic body can monomorphize another package's generic it reaches. Want: 42. See claude-todo.md.
